  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Captain Guy Hardy MacCaw served as a General Staff Officer during the First World War. After attending the Royal Military College, he was commissioned into the 17th Lancers in 1905 and subsequently served with the 3rd Hussars. He received Russia’s Order of Saint Vladimir, fourth class, with swords and bow.\n\nMacCaw was awarded the Military Cross in 1917 while holding the temporary rank of captain. Military service continued in the next generation: his son Derek became a Royal Air Force fighter pilot with 238 Squadron. Derek was killed in action over the English Channel during the Battle of Britain.",
    "html": "<p>Captain Guy Hardy MacCaw served as a General Staff Officer during the First World War. After attending the Royal Military College, he was commissioned into the 17th Lancers in 1905 and subsequently served with the 3rd Hussars. He received Russia’s Order of Saint Vladimir, fourth class, with swords and bow.</p>\r\n<p>MacCaw was awarded the Military Cross in 1917 while holding the temporary rank of captain. Military service continued in the next generation: his son Derek became a Royal Air Force fighter pilot with 238 Squadron. Derek was killed in action over the English Channel during the Battle of Britain.</p>\r\n",
